    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40-a1">

                <pb facs="0149" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg61"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 320.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Errazuriz to Mr. Egan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive the
                    communication of your excellency dated 2d instant, in which, after repeating
                    that stated by your excellency to this department on a former occasion with
                    reference to certain comments made by the press on <pb facs="0150" n="62"
                        xml:id="pg62"/> the conduct observed by Admiral Brown during the
                    disembarkation of the constitutional forces at Quinteros, your excellency
                    incloses a printed cutting in which the ex-governor of Quillota under the
                    Balmaceda administration explains the manner in which the knowledge of the
                    disembarkation of the said forces reached the authorities.</p>
                <p>I have taken careful note of the dispatch of your excellency, which I have read
                    with marked interest, and in acknowledging the receipt of it to your excellency
                    I am glad to avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Isidoro
                    Errazuriz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
